"settings.tab.help" = "Help";
"settings.help.whatsNewTitle" = "What's New";
"settings.help.whatsNewBody" = "v1.24.2 — Dictation cleanup no longer cold-starts the local MLX model after transcription: the on-device server already warmed up while you were speaking for the Whisper/Parakeet engine, but not for the AI cleanup step when it was pinned to MLX via a per-prompt override (auto-start at app launch only covered the global default provider). Now both warm up together, so loading overlaps with your recording instead of stalling after it finishes.\n\nv1.24.1 — Small icon polish: two success checkmarks (copy toast + local-model setup) now animate with a gentle bounce instead of appearing static.\n\nv1.24.0 — The update window now reliably comes to the front: as a menu-bar-only app Tippi has no Dock icon to signal a waiting update, so a window sitting behind a large one was simply never seen. It is now actively raised once it exists (the previous attempt failed because Sparkle creates the window only after the signal fires). Afterwards it behaves normally and can be left open. Also: the \"Model may be outdated\" warning now has a \"Switch to <model>\" button — the suggestion is checked against the same live catalogue that reported the problem, so it can never propose another dead model.\n\nv1.23.0 — Model catalogue audited and updated: a full check against every provider's own documentation found four of the nine cloud providers on stale or already-deprecated defaults. OpenAI's entire gpt-4o/gpt-5 line no longer exists (now gpt-5.6 Luna/Terra/Sol), Groq deprecated both Llama models Tippi used in June 2026 (now GPT-OSS), and two Anthropic presets were a generation behind (now Sonnet 5 / Opus 5). Gemini now uses the auto-updating alias \"gemini-flash-latest\" instead of a pinned version — the very property that carried Mistral through every retirement wave untouched. All dead ids are migrated automatically on next launch. Note: Claude Haiku 4.5 remains the fastest, cheapest recommendation, but Anthropic lists its retirement as no sooner than 2026-10-15.\n\nv1.22.1 — Fixed false \"model may be outdated\" warnings: the v1.21.0 check fetched each model list without a page size — Anthropic returns only 20 entries by default (newest first), so a perfectly working claude-haiku-4-5 was reported as retired. It now requests the full catalogue, refuses to warn at all on an incomplete one, and treats alias names (claude-haiku-4-5 vs. claude-haiku-4-5-20251001) as a match. New: a \"Which model for what?\" Help section with concrete recommendations.\n\nv1.22.0 — Language detection fixed + better prompts: on short text Tippi could detect the wrong language and then instruct the AI to stay in it — \"LG Michael\" was read as Polish, \"CINEWEB\" too, and when nothing was detected the prompt literally said \"Stay in .\". Now gated by a confidence threshold with a sensible fallback. Also: Shorten, Summarize, Email reply, Make Formal and Humanize now carry concrete before/after examples, which helps small local models most. New in Help: an explicit privacy note that {clipboard} sends your clipboard contents to your AI provider.\n\nv1.21.1 — The launch-time model check (v1.21.0) now runs at explicit background priority so it never competes with a hotkey press right after launch.\n\nv1.21.0 — OpenRouter + proactive model warning: New 11th provider OpenRouter — one key, 300+ models across every major vendor, model format \"vendor/model\". Tippi also now checks in the background at launch whether your configured model still exists at each provider, flagging it in Settings instead of you finding out via a failed real task (a direct response to the gemini-2.5 incident). The retired-model migration logic (previously Nebius-only) is now generalized and also reaches per-prompt provider overrides.\n\nv1.20.4 — Gemini model IDs updated: Google is retiring the 2.5 generation ahead of its official Oct 2026 shutdown — `gemini-2.5-flash` and `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` started returning \"no longer available to new users\" (HTTP 404). The default and fastest preset now point to `gemini-3.5-flash` / `gemini-3.5-flash-lite`. `gemini-2.5-pro` left unchanged (no reliable 3.x replacement confirmed) — flagged in the provider picker as possibly affected too.\n\nv1.20.3 — Switch provider right at the result: the preview now has a \"Switch provider\" menu in the footer — pick a different provider the moment a result disappoints you, and Tippi reruns immediately. Remembers the choice for that prompt (same storage as the Settings picker) — no detour through Settings needed. Not available for prompt chains, which resolve each step separately.\n\nv1.20.2 — Per-prompt provider override + \"no change\" hint: Settings → Prompts → Built-in now shows a provider picker for each of the 24 prompts instead of just \"read-only\" — useful when a small local model changes too little for a specific prompt (real case: \"Improve\" returned a long business email completely unchanged). If a prompt's result comes back identical to the original, the preview now shows a hint badge instead of letting it look like a normal result.\n\nv1.20.1 — Sharper dictation polish: the optional AI cleanup (Settings → Voice → Dictation) now recognizes filler words per language (German/English/Spanish/French/Japanese) instead of mixing them — words like English \"also\" (meaning \"in addition\") are no longer mistakenly stripped as filler. New: hesitation repeats are removed (\"the the file\" → \"the file\"), and German nouns are reliably capitalized.\n\nv1.20.0 — System audio muting: a new option under Settings → Voice → System Audio mutes your Mac's output for the duration of a recording (dictation, voice command, translate) and restores the exact previous state afterward. Off by default. Also: the built-in \"Improve\" prompt now names concrete edits instead of vague guidance.\n\nFull history: CHANGELOG.md in the project repository.";
"settings.help.howTitle" = "How Tippi works";
"settings.help.howBody" = "Select text in any app, then press your hotkey (default ⌥⌘T). A popup appears near your cursor — pick a prompt, preview the result, and replace or copy.";
"settings.help.instructTitle" = "Give an instruction — type or speak";
"settings.help.instructBody" = "Besides the built-in prompts, you can give Tippi a free-form instruction for the selected text. Trigger Tippi with text selected — an input field sits at the bottom of the popup. Type your instruction (e.g. \"reply to this email politely\", \"translate to Spanish\") and press Return, or tap the mic button and speak it. Tippi follows the instruction literally: transform instructions (translate, summarize, shorten) operate on the text as-is, while reaction instructions (reply, respond) produce an answer. The field auto-focuses so you can type right away; press ↓ to jump back to the prompt list.";
"settings.help.previewTitle" = "Live preview & refine";
"settings.help.previewBody" = "The result streams in token by token, so you see it forming instead of waiting for the whole answer. Once it's ready you can refine it in place: type a follow-up in the \"Refine\" field (e.g. \"shorter\", \"more formal\", \"add a greeting\") and it rewrites the current result — chain as many refinements as you like. Keyboard shortcuts in the preview: Return = Replace, ⌘C = Copy, ⌘Return = Append, ⌘R = Regenerate, Esc = Cancel. If a result hits the model's length limit it's kept but flagged \"Cut off\" so you don't replace a truncated text by accident.";
"settings.help.promptsTitle" = "Custom prompts";
"settings.help.promptsBody" = "Go to the Prompts tab to add your own. Each prompt needs a title, an SF Symbol name, and an instruction for the AI. The selected text is sent automatically — no placeholder needed.";
"settings.help.chainsTitle" = "Prompt chains";
"settings.help.chainsBody" = "In the prompt editor switch the type to Chain to run several prompts in a row. Each step's output feeds the next — e.g. Cleanup → English translates your text after fixing grammar. The preview shows the current step; if a step fails, the last good result stays editable. Try the built-in \"Cleanup → English\".";
"settings.help.localActionsTitle" = "Local quick actions";
"settings.help.localActionsBody" = "Tippi is not PopClip: marking text alone does not open the menu. Select text, then press your hotkey (default ⌥⌘T) or choose Trigger Tippi… from the menu bar.\n\nWhen text is captured, Quick actions appear above the AI prompts. They run locally: rich-text formatting, case changes, underscore/hyphen, brackets, join lines, and counts.\n\nBold/Italic/Underline/Strike use RTF when the app supports it; plain-text apps get Markdown-style fallbacks (**bold**, ~~struck~~). Counts only show a number and do not edit text.\n\nIf you see “No text captured”, grant Accessibility for the Tippi.app you launched (local test builds need a fresh toggle after each make build). TextEdit and Notes work best. Hide Quick actions in Settings → General.";
"settings.help.troubleBody" = "Nothing happens when you only highlight text? Press ⌥⌘T (or ⌃⌥⌘T) after selecting — Tippi does not auto-open like PopClip.\n\nHotkey not firing? Grant Accessibility (System Settings → Privacy & Security → Accessibility). Trigger via menu bar ✏️ → Trigger Tippi…\n\nQuick actions show but text does not change? Re-select text in TextEdit/Notes, trigger again, then tap the action. Local builds: enable Accessibility for build/Build/Products/Release/Tippi.app and restart the app.\n\nNew hotkey not responding? Quit and reopen Tippi.";
"settings.help.variablesTitle" = "Prompt variables";
"settings.help.variablesBody" = "Use {placeholders} in your prompt instructions — Tippi fills them in at trigger time:\n\n{clipboard} — your current clipboard content\n{app_name} — the app you're writing in (e.g. Mail, Safari, Slack)\n{language} — detected language of your selected text (e.g. German)\n{selected_text} — the selected text itself\n\nExample — app-aware tone:\n\"Rewrite for {app_name}. In Slack: casual, max 2 sentences. In Mail: formal.\"\n\nExample — clipboard as style reference (copy a sample text first):\n\"Match the tone of this reference: {clipboard}\"\n\nExample — always stay in the right language:\n\"Improve the text. Stay in {language}. Return only the result.\"\n\n⚠️ Privacy note on {clipboard}: whatever is in your clipboard becomes part of the prompt and is therefore sent to your AI provider. Don't use this placeholder while a password, API key or other sensitive data is copied — or pick a local provider (MLX/Ollama) for such prompts, where nothing leaves your Mac.";
"settings.help.importExportTitle" = "Share & import prompts";
"settings.help.importExportBody" = "Export your custom prompts as a .tippipack file to share them with teammates or keep a backup.\n\nExport all — click \"Export All\" at the top of the Prompts tab.\nExport one — click the ↑ icon next to any prompt.\nImport — click \"Import\", select a .tippipack file, then choose Merge (keeps your existing prompts) or Replace (replaces them).\n\nImported prompts always get fresh IDs, so they never conflict with existing ones.";
"settings.help.apiTitle" = "AI providers & keys";
"settings.help.apiBody" = "Add your API key in the Providers tab. Tippi supports 11 providers — OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Mistral, Scaleway (EU, Paris), Groq, Kimi/Moonshot, Nebius (EU, Amsterdam) and OpenRouter (300+ models behind one key) as cloud BYOK providers, plus Ollama and MLX (both fully local, free, no key needed). Keys are stored securely in the macOS Keychain.\n\nDefault provider: Tippi tries your chosen default first; if it has no key it falls through to the next configured one. With no explicit default it automatically uses the first provider you've added a key for, so a fresh install never stalls on a cold local model. Optional fallback (Providers tab): if your provider fails (rate limit, server or network error) Tippi can retry the next configured provider — off by default since it sends your text to a second provider.";

"settings.help.linksTitle" = "Links & resources";
"settings.help.linksBody" = "[GitHub repository](https://github.com/miwixyz/Tippi) — public, MIT-licensed, source code, issues, releases.\n\n[Landing page](https://miwixyz.github.io/Tippi/) — bilingual EN/DE, features, screenshots, download.\n\n[One-pager](https://github.com/miwixyz/Tippi/blob/main/docs/ONE-PAGER.md) — for Hacker News, Reddit, sharing with friends; what Tippi is in 60 seconds.\n\n[Changelog](https://github.com/miwixyz/Tippi/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md) — every change, every version.\n\n[Latest release](https://github.com/miwixyz/Tippi/releases/latest) — DMG download, release notes, checksums.";

